    "title": "Computer vision",
    "description": "Wikipedia article about Computer vision",
    "document": "WIKI/computer_vision.md",
    "chunk_text": "useful in order to receive accurate data on imperfections on a very large surface. Another variation of this finger mold sensor are sensors that contain a camera suspended in silicon. The silicon forms a dome around the outside of the camera and embedded in the silicon are point markers that are equally spaced. These cameras can then be placed on devices such as robotic hands in order to allow the computer to receive highly accurate tactile data. Other application areas include:  Support of visual effects creation for cinema and broadcast, e.g., camera tracking (match moving). Surveillance. Driver drowsiness detection Tracking and counting organisms in the biological sciences  Typical tasks Each of the application areas described above",
    "chunk_token_count": 116,
